112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 80 0 R
/E (Most recipe and diet-tracking applications recommend meals based only on available ingredients or dietary restrictions, overlooking the user's mood and situational context. MoodMeal is a desktop application, developed using Java \(Swing/JavaFX\) and MySQL, that recommends recipes based on the user's current mood, available pantry ingredients, and basic nutritional goals. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 80 0 R
/E (Recipes are tagged with mood-suitability scores, nutrition values, and ingredients, allowing users to receive filtered suggestions displayed as visual cards with prep time and a "comfort vs. energy" rating. The system also tracks mood-to-meal history, revealing simple eating patterns over time through basic charts. The project applies core Java concepts, JDBC-based MySQL CRUD operations, and GUI design to an underexplored intersection of nutrition and emotional wellbeing.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
