118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (Emotional eating is a well-documented behavioral pattern, where stress, fatigue, boredom, or celebration often drive people toward specific types of food, such as comfort food during stressful periods or lighter meals when energy is low. Existing nutrition and recipe platforms largely overlook this connection, leaving a gap between how people actually decide what to eat and how technology tries to help them decide. MoodMeal is designed to address this gap directly, bridging nutrition technology with emotional wellbeing by incorporating the user's mood as a core factor in generating recipe recommendations, alongside available ingredients and nutritional goals.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
